on as the first-ever female gold medalist in track and field, winning the 100m sprint at just 16 years old. However, three years later, her career—and her life—seemed to end in a horrific plane crash. A passerby pulled her from the wreckage and, finding no pulse and seeing her devastating injuries, concluded she was dead. He didn't want to leave a \"body\" in the field, so he lifted her limp frame and shoved it into the trunk of his car to drive her to the local undertaker.In an incredible twist, the \"corpse\" began to stir just as she arrived at the mortuary. X had survived, but she was in a coma for seven months and her injuries were so severe that one of her legs was now significantly shorter than the other. Doctors told her she would never walk again, let alone run. Yet, because she could no longer crouch into the standard \"starting blocks\" position, she spent the next five years training to sprint from a standing start. In 1936, she returned to the Olympics in Berlin and won her second gold medal.What was the bizarre \"near-death\" experience that almost saw this Olympic champion buried alive?", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-30T15:38:43Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "betty", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-30T15:38:54Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "Vats: 50, Kp: 50, Khandoba: 10, Tapish: 5, Gautam: 5", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-30T15:39:07Z", "username": "Chinmay Mehta", "text": "Half century each for vatapy, kptapy", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-30T15:39:15Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Verstappen goes on the outside and takes the lead", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-30T15:39:29Z",